      "writtenOn": "2026-09-07T23:59:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I\u0027m not sure what for.\n\nThe motivation was to avoid calling `pkvm_host_share_hyp` and `pkvm_host_unshare_hyp` for this short duration usecase. We can achieve share-\u003ecopy-\u003eunshare with this single api. And it makes the code simpler.\n\nFor eg: GSMI_CMD_SET_EVENT_LOG can then be simplified as:\n\n```\ncase GSMI_CMD_SET_EVENT_LOG: {\n\t\tstruct gsmi_set_eventlog_param *sel;\n\t\tstruct gsmi_log_entry_type_1 *type1;\n\t\t\n\t\tsel \u003d \u0026this_cpu_read(bounce_ptr)-\u003eset_eventlog;\n\t\ttype1 \u003d \u0026this_cpu_read(bounce_ptr)-\u003elog_entry;\n\n\t\tif (pkvm_copy_from_host(sel, pkvm_host_gpa_to_virt(param), sizeof(*sel)))\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\n\t\tif (sel-\u003etype !\u003d 1) {\n\t\t\tret \u003d GSMI_UNSUPPORTED;\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif (!sel-\u003edata_ptr || sel-\u003edata_len !\u003d sizeof(*type1))\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\n\t\tif (pkvm_copy_from_host(type1, pkvm_host_gpa_to_virt(sel-\u003edata_ptr), sizeof(*type1)))\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\n\t\tsel-\u003edata_ptr \u003d __pkvm_pa(type1);\n\n\t\tret \u003d gsmi_write(subcmd, __pkvm_pa(sel));\n\t\tbreak;\n\t}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "fdde28aa_8ce5d556",
